Source change represented by patch_mgba.py for the validated arm64 binary.
Upstream source https://github.com/mgba-emu/mgba/blob/0.10.5/src/script/socket.c
Original source copyright Jeffrey Pfau, Mozilla Public License 2.0.

--- a/src/script/socket.c
+++ b/src/script/socket.c
@@
 void _mScriptSocketClose(struct mScriptSocket* ssock) {
     if (!SOCKET_FAILED(ssock->socket)) {
-        SocketClose(ssock->socket);
+        Socket descriptor = ssock->socket;
+        ssock->socket = INVALID_SOCKET;
+        SocketClose(descriptor);
     }
 }

The binary form sets INVALID_SOCKET immediately before close(fd). Both the
explicit close call and the userdata destructor then preserve idempotency.

--- a/src/script/socket.c
+++ b/src/script/socket.c
@@
-    if (bytes <= 0) {
+    if (bytes < 0) {
         data->size = 0;
         _mScriptSocketSetError(ssock, SocketError());
     } else {
         data->size = bytes;
         ssock->error = mSCRIPT_SOCKERR_OK;
     }

A zero-length receive represents EOF and clears stale errno-derived errors.
Both exported and compiler-inlined binding implementations are checked.
